course: dictionary
lesson: 15577
title: A green word for grass
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sward is an old word. You will mostly meet it in poems and older stories about the countryside. It means an area of short grass, like a lawn or a green field covered in turf.
explain: «The rabbits hopped across the green sward.» The clues are green and rabbits hopping, and rabbits hop on grass. So sward must mean grass. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The rabbits hopped across the green lawn» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Sward is a noun, so it names a thing. Its plural is swards, for more than one patch of grass. Look for words like green, short and smooth near it, because poets use them to paint a picture of the grass.
fact: Sward means an area of short grass, such as a lawn or a green field.
fact: Sward is an old, literary word, so you will mostly find it in poems and older stories.
fact: «A green sward» means a smooth, green patch of grass.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows there are meadows and green river banks, the kind of land a sward covers.
fact: In farming and geography, sward means the grass cover of a field.
exercise: «The children rolled down the sward and laughed.» What is a sward? | A muddy puddle | *An area of short grass | A stone wall by the road | A tall tree in a forest
exercise: «The children rolled down the sward and laughed.» Which word is closest in meaning to sward? | River | Castle | *Lawn | Whisper
exercise: Ella says sward is just a fancy word for mud. Why is she wrong? | Sward means a dark cave under the hill | Sward means a wet puddle | *Sward means short grass, not mud | Sward means a bag of sand
test: «We lay on the sward and watched the clouds drift by.» What does sward mean here? | Sandy beach | Sky | A kind of small boat | *Short grass
test: Why might a farmer look at the sward of a field? | To hear the wind | *To see how the grass is growing | To find the nearest shop | To count the trees on the hill
exam: Which of these describes a sward? | *A short, green lawn of grass | A tall, dark forest | A deep, cold river | A heavy bag of sand
